--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/lotus_v2/peer_tcp_test/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Nonblocking TCP byte stream
+
+This packet implements the existing `peer::ByteStream` interface with POSIX TCP
+on **Linux and macOS**. It creates no node, peer manager, chainstate, defaults,
+seeds, DNS resolver, profile selection or network activation. Root owns shared
+build registration; unsupported platforms must omit this implementation until a
+separately reviewed adapter exists.
+
+## Explicit API and ownership
+
+`ParseNumericEndpoint` accepts bounded IPv4/IPv6 literals through `inet_pton`,
+with caller-supplied port and IPv6 scope ID. Host names, embedded NUL, bracketed
+URLs and textual zone IDs are rejected. `TcpEndpoint{}` is Unspecified and cannot
+bind/connect. A wildcard address is possible only if explicitly supplied by the
+caller. Connect rejects port0; Listen accepts explicit port0 for OS ephemeral
+allocation. Backlog and IPv6-only policy are explicit arguments. No SO_REUSEPORT
+or SO_REUSEADDR option is silently installed.
+
+`TcpStream` and `TcpListener` each own at most one descriptor. They are move-only;
+move assignment deliberately releases the old owned descriptor. Failed
+BeginConnect/Listen on an open object preserves that connection/listener.
+Accept performs at most one accept syscall, refuses an open stream output before
+accepting, and publishes stream/remote outputs only after complete configuration.
+Failure and WouldBlock leave both outputs unchanged. BoundEndpoint similarly
+changes output only on success. NativeHandle is borrowed: never close it or
+change its nonblocking/close-on-exec flags.
+
+The existing Transport borrows the **stream object**, so never move, replace or
+destroy it while a Transport still references it. Destroy Transport first, or
+close it and keep the referenced stream object alive through Transport destruction.
+Transport cleanup and the stream's destructor are safe together because Close
+exchanges the descriptor to -1 before its single close syscall. Close never
+retries EINTR: POSIX close interruption can be ambiguous, and retrying a reused
+number could close another resource. Kernel disposition after such an ambiguous
+close is outside the close-once guarantee.
+
+Callers serialize access. No callbacks or heap buffers are stored by this adapter.
+On macOS close-on-exec/nonblocking configuration follows socket/accept through
+fcntl; callers must serialize concurrent fork/exec with that configuration
+window. Linux socket/accept4 also set those flags atomically. This packet installs
+no process-wide signal disposition. SIGPIPE is suppressed per send with Linux
+MSG_NOSIGNAL, or per socket with macOS SO_NOSIGPIPE before ownership publication.
+
+## Bounds and operation results
+
+Read/Write issue one syscall with span size capped at SSIZE_MAX. Partial progress
+is returned exactly. EINTR/EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK become WouldBlock with count0;
+EOF/Error also have count0. Empty spans or disconnected use produce Error.
+EOF alone retains descriptor ownership until explicit Close or destruction;
+Transport handles its own EOF cleanup. LastError is the latest operational POSIX
+errno, not protocol/consensus invalidity or a peer reputation decision.
+
+PollReadiness checks one descriptor with poll(timeout0). It does not sleep or
+implement a scheduler. BeginConnect and Listen perform a fixed sequence of at
+most ten syscalls, including configuration and failure cleanup; Accept at most
+seven. PollConnect performs at most poll+getsockopt+failure close. None loops on
+interruption. Connect completion
+uses SO_ERROR and a fixed caller-injected monotonic deadline. Zero/overflowing
+timeouts reject before creation; clock rollback closes a pending attempt;
+expiry closes it without extending for retries. Established streams have no
+adapter idle timeout; Session/Transport retain their separate deadlines.
+
+The caller must bound retained stream/listener objects, accept/connect attempts
+per scheduler turn, and transport action/byte budgets. Kernel backlog/socket
+buffers, caller-owned spans and Transport/Session queues have separate quotas.
+The explicit backlog is subject to OS clamping; no exact kernel-memory bound is
+claimed. This packet adds no unbounded descriptor collection or buffering.
+
+## Standalone checks
+
+```sh
+cmake -S src/lotus_v2/peer_tcp_test -B /tmp/lotus-v2-tcp-build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DLOTUS_SECP_LIBRARY=/absolute/path/libsecp256k1.a
+cmake --build /tmp/lotus-v2-tcp-build
+ctest --test-dir /tmp/lotus-v2-tcp-build --output-on-failure
+```
+
+Use a fresh build with `-DLOTUS_SANITIZE=ON` for ASan/UBSan on the executable's
+C++ sources. The separate BLAKE3 C library and supplied secp library are unchanged.
+
+Tests bind only numeric localhost IPv4/IPv6 with explicit ephemeral port0;
+10604/10605/8331 are never configured and returned ports are checked. They cover
+nonblocking/close-on-exec flags, connect/accept/read/write/EOF, partial progress,
+WouldBlock, duplicate bind and preserved refused outputs, deadline/rollback/
+overflow, refused connection, moves and descriptor reuse after repeated Close,
+bounded backpressure, actual EPIPE survival without a SIGPIPE handler, and the
+existing Transport handshake plus exact application bytes over fragmented real
+TCP. Every wait and send loop has a fixed iteration/byte cap. Deadline branches
+are exercised when the OS reports the connection pending rather than already
+connected. EINTR mapping is reviewed source behavior; tests do not force kernel
+signal interruption. These are source/local-socket checks, not daemon acceptance,
+public peering, synchronization, consensus validation or a selected testnet.
+
+Validated on macOS arm64; Linux implementation is source-reviewed, with execution
+on Linux still an integration/CI gate. No existing native files or shared build
+registration are changed by this packet.
+
+Packet evidence (2026-10-15), fresh native base `f93ea73fd`: focused Debug test
+1/1 passed in 0.46 seconds, and ASan+UBSan 1/1 passed in 0.40 seconds. Independent
+read-only source/ownership/borrowing review found no concrete blocker. No public
+endpoint was contacted and no fixed service port was configured.
diff --git a/src/lotus_v2/peer_transport.cpp b/src/lotus_v2/peer_transport.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4f6621df3d15db7c0eab2e696643993db41dde28
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/lotus_v2/peer_transport.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,322 @@
+// Copyright (c) 2026 The Lotus developers
+#include "peer_transport.h"
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <limits>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <utility>
+namespace lotus::v2::peer {
+namespace {
+    struct Guard {
+        bool &flag;
+        explicit Guard(bool &f) : flag(f) { flag = true; }
+        ~Guard() { flag = false; }
+    };
+} // namespace
+Transport::Transport(ByteStream &stream, SessionConfig config,
+                     TransportLimits limits)
+    : stream_(stream), network_(config.network), limits_(limits) {
+    if (!limits.read_chunk_bytes ||
+        limits.read_chunk_bytes > MAX_RECEIVE_LIMIT || !limits.outbound_bytes ||
+        !limits.outbound_frames || !limits.incomplete_frame_timeout_ms ||
+        !limits.queued_frame_timeout_ms)
+        throw std::invalid_argument(
+            "transport limits must be positive and read chunk bounded");
+    session_ = std::make_unique<Session>(std::move(config));
+    read_.resize(limits.read_chunk_bytes);
+}
+Transport::~Transport() noexcept {
+    busy_ = true;
+    Stop(TransportClose::Requested);
+}
+SessionState Transport::State() const {
+    return session_ ? session_->State() : SessionState::Closed;
+}
+uint32_t Transport::ActiveLimit() const {
+    return session_ ? session_->ActiveLimit() : 0;
+}
+void Transport::Stop(TransportClose reason) noexcept {
+    if (closed_ != TransportClose::None) return;
+    closed_ = reason;
+    // Destroy Session to release decoder allocation even if diagnostics cannot
+    // allocate. Cleanup never calls an allocation-producing OnClosed method.
+    session_.reset();
+    event_.reset();
+    outbound_.clear();
+    Bytes{}.swap(read_);
+    queued_bytes_ = read_begin_ = read_end_ = 0;
+    read_deadline_.reset();
+    stream_.Close();
+}
+bool Transport::Close() noexcept {
+    if (busy_) return false;
+    Guard guard(busy_);
+    Stop(TransportClose::Requested);
+    return true;
+}
+bool Transport::Deadline(uint64_t now, uint64_t duration, uint64_t &out) {
+    if (duration > UINT64_MAX - now) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+        return false;
+    }
+    out = now + duration;
+    return true;
+}
+bool Transport::Time(uint64_t now) {
+    if (closed_ != TransportClose::None) return false;
+    if (!opened_ || now < last_ms_) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+        return false;
+    }
+    last_ms_ = now;
+    if ((read_deadline_ && now >= *read_deadline_) ||
+        (!outbound_.empty() && now >= outbound_.front().deadline)) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::TimedOut);
+        return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+bool Transport::Handle(SessionEvent event, uint64_t now) {
+    switch (event.result) {
+        case SessionResult::PeerRejected:
+            Stop(TransportClose::PeerRejected);
+            return false;
+        case SessionResult::LocalFailure:
+            Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+            return false;
+        case SessionResult::TimedOut:
+            Stop(TransportClose::TimedOut);
+            return false;
+        case SessionResult::Closed:
+            Stop(TransportClose::Requested);
+            return false;
+        default:
+            break;
+    }
+    size_t extra = 0;
+    if (event.outbound.size() > limits_.outbound_frames - outbound_.size()) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::Capacity);
+        return false;
+    }
+    for (const auto &frame : event.outbound) {
+        if (frame.size() > limits_.outbound_bytes - queued_bytes_ - extra) {
+            Stop(TransportClose::Capacity);
+            return false;
+        }
+        extra += frame.size();
+    }
+    if (!event.outbound.empty()) {
+        uint64_t deadline;
+        if (!Deadline(now, limits_.queued_frame_timeout_ms, deadline))
+            return false;
+        for (auto &frame : event.outbound)
+            outbound_.push_back({std::move(frame), 0, deadline});
+        queued_bytes_ += extra;
+    }
+    event.outbound.clear();
+    if (event.result == SessionResult::Application ||
+        event.result == SessionResult::Activated)
+        event_ = std::move(event);
+    return true;
+}
+bool Transport::Open(uint64_t now) {
+    if (busy_ || closed_ != TransportClose::None) return false;
+    Guard guard(busy_);
+    if (opened_) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+        return false;
+    }
+    opened_ = true;
+    last_ms_ = now;
+    try {
+        return Handle(session_->OnOpen(now), now);
+    } catch (...) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+        return false;
+    }
+}
+QueueResult Transport::QueueMessage(const Message &message, uint64_t now) {
+    if (busy_) return QueueResult::Busy;
+    Guard guard(busy_);
+    if (!Time(now)) return QueueResult::Closed;
+    if (State() != SessionState::Active) return QueueResult::NotActive;
+    if (AvalancheCommand(message.command) && !(ActiveFeatures() & AVALANCHE_FEATURE))
+        return QueueResult::InvalidMessage;
+    // Preflight checked 24-byte overhead before the codec copies or allocates.
+    if (message.payload.size() > std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max() - 24)
+        return QueueResult::Backpressure;
+    const size_t bytes = 24 + message.payload.size();
+    if (outbound_.size() >= limits_.outbound_frames ||
+        bytes > limits_.outbound_bytes - queued_bytes_)
+        return QueueResult::Backpressure;
+    uint64_t deadline;
+    if (!Deadline(now, limits_.queued_frame_timeout_ms, deadline))
+        return QueueResult::Closed;
+    try {
+        Bytes frame;
+        std::string error;
+        if (!EncodeEnvelope(network_, ActiveLimit(), message, frame, error))
+            return QueueResult::InvalidMessage;
+        outbound_.push_back({std::move(frame), 0, deadline});
+        queued_bytes_ += bytes;
+        return QueueResult::Queued;
+    } catch (...) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+        return QueueResult::Closed;
+    }
+}
+std::optional<SessionEvent> Transport::TakeEvent() {
+    if (busy_) return std::nullopt;
+    Guard guard(busy_);
+    auto event = std::move(event_);
+    event_.reset();
+    return event;
+}
+bool Transport::Valid(const StreamResult &result, size_t authorized) {
+    bool valid =
+        result.status == StreamStatus::Progress
+            ? result.count > 0 && result.count <= authorized
+            : result.count == 0 && (result.status == StreamStatus::WouldBlock ||
+                                    result.status == StreamStatus::Eof ||
+                                    result.status == StreamStatus::Error);
+    if (!valid) Stop(TransportClose::StreamContract);
+    return valid;
+}
+TransportPoll Transport::Poll(uint64_t now, const TransportBudget &budget) {
+    TransportPoll report;
+    if (busy_) {
+        report.busy = true;
+        return report;
+    }
+    Guard guard(busy_);
+    auto done = [&] {
+        report.closed = closed_;
+        report.event_pending = event_.has_value();
+        return report;
+    };
+    if (!Time(now)) return done();
+    // At least one action is necessary to service Session's timer. Zero budget
+    // is a caller operational error, not a peer protocol failure.
+    if (!budget.max_actions) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+        return done();
+    }
+    try {
+        ++report.actions;
+        if (!Handle(session_->OnTimer(now), now)) return done();
+        size_t io_authorized = 0;
+        bool read_blocked = false, write_blocked = false;
+        while (report.actions < budget.max_actions) {
+            bool worked = false;
+            // Output gets one bounded attempt per iteration; a blocked write
+            // does not block receive/handshake progress.
+            if (!write_blocked && !outbound_.empty() &&
+                io_authorized < budget.max_io_bytes) {
+                auto &frame = outbound_.front();
+                const size_t n = std::min(frame.bytes.size() - frame.sent,
+                                          budget.max_io_bytes - io_authorized);
+                ++report.actions;
+                ++report.io_calls;
+                const auto result =
+                    stream_.Write(std::span<const uint8_t>(frame.bytes)
+                                      .subspan(frame.sent, n));
+                if (!Valid(result, n)) return done();
+                if (result.status == StreamStatus::Progress) {
+                    io_authorized += result.count;
+                    frame.sent += result.count;
+                    report.written_bytes += result.count;
+                    if (frame.sent == frame.bytes.size()) {
+                        queued_bytes_ -= frame.bytes.size();
+                        outbound_.pop_front();
+                    }
+                    worked = true;
+                } else if (result.status == StreamStatus::WouldBlock) {
+                    report.write_blocked = write_blocked = true;
+                } else {
+                    Stop(result.status == StreamStatus::Eof
+                             ? TransportClose::EndOfStream
+                             : TransportClose::StreamError);
+                    return done();
+                }
+            }
+            if (report.actions >= budget.max_actions) break;
+            if (!event_ && read_begin_ < read_end_ &&
+                report.fed_bytes < budget.max_feed_bytes) {
+                const size_t n =
+                    std::min(read_end_ - read_begin_,
+                             budget.max_feed_bytes - report.fed_bytes);
+                size_t consumed = 0;
+                ++report.actions;
+                auto event = session_->Feed(
+                    std::span<const uint8_t>(read_).subspan(read_begin_, n),
+                    now, consumed);
+                if (consumed > n ||
+                    (consumed == 0 && event.result == SessionResult::Idle)) {
+                    Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+                    return done();
+                }
+                read_begin_ += consumed;
+                report.fed_bytes += consumed;
+                // Any non-Idle successful event marks a complete envelope.
+                if (event.result != SessionResult::Idle) {
+                    read_deadline_.reset();
+                    if (read_begin_ < read_end_) {
+                        uint64_t deadline;
+                        if (!Deadline(read_arrival_ms_,
+                                      limits_.incomplete_frame_timeout_ms,
+                                      deadline))
+                            return done();
+                        read_deadline_ = deadline;
+                    }
+                }
+                if (read_begin_ == read_end_) read_begin_ = read_end_ = 0;
+                if (!Handle(std::move(event), now)) return done();
+                worked = true;
+            }
+            if (report.actions >= budget.max_actions) break;
+            if (!event_ && !read_blocked && read_end_ == 0 &&
+                io_authorized < budget.max_io_bytes) {
+                const size_t n =
+                    std::min(read_.size(), budget.max_io_bytes - io_authorized);
+                ++report.actions;
+                ++report.io_calls;
+                auto result = stream_.Read(std::span<uint8_t>(read_).first(n));
+                if (!Valid(result, n)) return done();
+                if (result.status == StreamStatus::Progress) {
+                    io_authorized += result.count;
+                    read_arrival_ms_ = now;
+                    read_end_ = result.count;
+                    report.read_bytes += result.count;
+                    if (!read_deadline_) {
+                        uint64_t deadline;
+                        if (!Deadline(read_arrival_ms_,
+                                      limits_.incomplete_frame_timeout_ms,
+                                      deadline))
+                            return done();
+                        read_deadline_ = deadline;
+                    }
+                    worked = true;
+                } else if (result.status == StreamStatus::WouldBlock) {
+                    report.read_blocked = read_blocked = true;
+                } else {
+                    Stop(result.status == StreamStatus::Eof
+                             ? TransportClose::EndOfStream
+                             : TransportClose::StreamError);
+                    return done();
+                }
+            }
+            if (!worked) break;
+        }
+    } catch (...) {
+        Stop(TransportClose::LocalFailure);
+    }
+    return done();
+}
+} // namespace lotus::v2::peer
+
+uint64_t lotus::v2::peer::Transport::ActiveFeatures() const {
+    return session_ ? session_->ActiveFeatures() : 0;
+}
+
+std::optional<lotus::v2::peer::NegotiatedTranscript> lotus::v2::peer::Transport::Transcript() const {
+    return session_ ? session_->Transcript() : std::nullopt;
+}
